          "y": "20.0",
          "w": "640"
        },
        "parms": "# flush and midiflush — a panic button for stuck notes\nA note that is switched on and never switched off keeps sounding: a stuck note. It happens when a patch stops in the middle of a phrase. flush and midiflush pass notes through and remember which are still sounding, and a bang releases exactly those.\nflush watches pitch and velocity pairs, before they become MIDI, and releases a note with velocity 0. midiflush watches the MIDI messages on their way to midiout, and sends a note-off for each note on the channel it was played on. When the patch closes, both release their notes first.\nmidiout's argument is the output port, counted from 0; the midiinfo tutorial lists them. You hear something only when a synthesizer listens on that port.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
